! DR-A Task 2.2e_og Diffusion of Cs+ 
!        Based on the approach of PSI in the presentation at Mont Terri workshop (Dec. 2012)      
!    effective porosity 0.15
!    composition of pore water 
!   and sorption properties see paper van Loon et al. (2009),
!   applied geochemistry 24, 999-1004, model II.
!
! set up on Dec 3, 2012 MX   
!   
!    
!    1. dry bulk density of clay 2.4 -> 2.2295 (similiar to Mt Terri TR 2009-04) 
!    2. The gap between filter and clay is open, no filling, no sorption in gap

! 
! list modified. April 21, 2013 MX, correct radius of BH, 
!              Filter and gap by factor alpha = 4.16/3.80
!              r'_BH=0.0339m, r'_filter=0.0383, por_BH=2.976
!  modified April 16, 2013 after meeting: Porosity of iBH=3.567
! last modified: according to PSI, use Cl- for charge balance, 
!     
!    scaling according to PSI, Porosity of iBH=3.262 (using solution volume 10.243)
!  Tau correction according to PSI	
!    for Cs simulation: D0=1.0e-9m^2/s, Dp=2.7e-10m^2/s	
!    tau=Dp/D0=	0.27
!    Ion exchange (one site - type II model only)
!
!  Increase Dp of Cs to 1.3e-9m^2/s (i.e. tau=0.5, D0=2.6e-9m^2/s)	
!
!! last modified, Oct 21, 2013: according to PSI, multisite ion exchange model, 
!     with site fractions FES 1.05e-4 eq/kg, type-II 8.4e-3 eq/kg, and PS 0.095eq/kg

! Data Block 1: global control parameters
! ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
!
'global control parameters'
'Title: Task 2.2e_og Diffusion of HTO and Co-60'
.true.                        ;varsat_flow
.true.                        ;steady_flow
.true.                        ;fully_saturated
.true.                        ;reactive_transport

'hybrid multicomponent diffusion'

'parallel solver configuration file'
'solver.cfg'

'done'

